# Google pkcs11test tests left out for libkythira_pkcs11.so, one gtest
# pattern per line, each with the reason. consumers.sh joins them into
# --gtest_filter=-<patterns>. Only behaviour the virtual HSM leaves out by
# design belongs here (.kiro/specs/virtual-hsm/ requirement 6.5 and
# mechanisms.hpp's unsupported_functions()); a failure anywhere else is a
# bug to fix, not a line to add.
#
# pkcs11test (commit 2cbe462c) builds most of its fixtures from keys the
# virtual HSM does not make: SecretKey() defaults to CKM_DES3_KEY_GEN and
# KeyPair() asks for a 1024-bit RSA modulus. Its cipher table is DES,
# 3DES, AES-ECB and AES-CBC without padding. Requirement 6 keeps the
# mechanism list to AES-GCM, AES-CBC-PAD, AES key wrap, RSA of 2048 bits
# or more, EC and HMAC, so every test below fails at its fixture or at
# C_EncryptInit with CKR_MECHANISM_INVALID or CKR_KEY_SIZE_RANGE before
# it reaches what it means to check.

# DES, 3DES, AES-ECB and unpadded AES-CBC: the whole cipher table.
Ciphers/SecretKeyTest.*
# Fixture: a 3DES secret key.
Digests/DigestTest.DigestKey*
Duals/DualSecretKeyTest.*
ROUserSessionTest.WrapUnwrap
ROUserSessionTest.WrapInvalid
ROUserSessionTest.UnwrapInvalid
RWEitherSessionTest.TookanAttackA2
ReadWriteSessionTest.TookanAttack*
ReadWriteSessionTest.FindObjectSubset
ReadWriteSessionTest.SetLatchingAttribute
# C_CreateObject of CKK_DES keys and DES/3DES test vectors.
ReadOnlySessionTest.CreateSecretKeyAttributes
ReadOnlySessionTest.SecretKeyTestVectors
# Fixture or test vectors: RSA with a 1024-bit modulus.
Signatures/SignTest.*
KeyPairTest.EncryptDecrypt
ReadOnlySessionTest.CreateKeyPairObjects
ReadOnlySessionTest.SignVerifyRecover
ReadWriteSessionTest.PublicExponent4Bytes
ReadWriteSessionTest.ExtractKeys
ReadWriteSessionTest.AsymmetricTokenKeyPair
